  "issue_title": "Track judge-order telemetry across replay runs",
  "issue_body": "**Context**\nThis PR exposes per-run dual-order disagreement telemetry, which lets us distinguish model parity from judge instability inside a single replay. The next useful step is to preserve that signal across runs so maintainers can spot judge drift, prompt regressions, or cost/variance changes over time.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- [ ] Persist `judge_order_stats` in any replay history or CI artifact format we already publish.\n- [ ] Add a lightweight regression check or report line for `disagreement_rate` when dual-order judging is enabled.\n- [ ] Document how maintainers should interpret a rising disagreement rate.\n\n**Pointers**: `benchmark/runner.py`, `benchmark/judge.py`, replay result serialization/reporting code",
